Subject: [PATCH 4/6] J714s image line on 27.2: board Mach-O Stage 1
 (board-macho-ctxr-v1), confined Stage 2, omarchy-j714s-N

The j714s-developer profile (27.3 stub, common raw Stage 1) becomes the j714s
profile: the one J714s image line, booted from macOS 27.2 stub firmware through
Aura's padded Mach-O Stage 1 (SPTM off, CTXR execute window).

- stage1_qualification: a new kind, board-macho-ctxr-v1, next to common-raw-v1:
  one known board on its one OS firmware (j714sap on 27.2), no system firmware
  pin. The J714s budgets now need exactly that profile. The 27.2 kernel pin is
  7.3.0.aurora17.v272-1 / 7.3.0-17.v272-1-ARCH, from the linux-aurora-j714s
  recipe before its first build.
- The image carries esp/aurora/stage1-j714s.bin (m1n1-aurora's raw Stage 1),
  esp/aurora/stage1-j714s.macho (aura's MH_FILESET wrap of it: m1n1-boot.macho,
  else m1n1.macho) and esp/m1n1/boot-ctxr.bin, and no stage1.bin or J700 pair.
  builder/aura_macho.py holds the object to the engine's rules (raw Stage 1 at
  the start of __TEXT_EXEC, zeros after, entry at +0x800, no __TEXT_BOOT_EXEC).
- boot-ctxr.bin is made right after update-m1n1 by the profile's helper: a copy
  of m1n1/boot.bin (m1n1-aurora's m1n1.bin is the ESP_STAGE2=1 build), or
  m1n1-ctxr.bin + boot.bin's tail after m1n1.bin when a package ships it apart.
  Its pacman hook, 96-omarchy-j714s-boot-ctxr.hook (after asahi-scripts'
  95-m1n1-install.hook, same targets), keeps it current on the installed system.
- installer_data: allowed_device_classes [j714sap], aurora_stage1 board-macho-ctxr-v1,
  supported_fw [27.2], next_object stays m1n1/boot.bin (the engine picks
  boot-ctxr.bin from the kind), recovery_gui omarchy-native-v1.
- Payload omarchy-j714s-<N>-aarch64-apple-silicon-mac-os-package.zip, N from
  --image-version / MAC_IMAGE_VERSION (default 1); IMAGE and PROVENANCE record
  image_line and image_version and mac-image-check holds the name to them. The
  line has no lab variant.
- Inspection checks the Stage 1 pair against the set's m1n1-aurora, boot-ctxr.bin
  against boot.bin (or the m1n1-ctxr.bin splice), and the helper and hook bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
